I found that I had screen 3.9.11 in my rather plain-vanilla SuSE 8
setup, so I took it for a spin.

What a mess.

It doesn't support IBMgraphics at all.  It *almost* supports DECgraphics
but you wind up with a square (as IBMgraphics shows for an open door)
instead of the dot that is supposed to be the floor.

Perhaps DECgraphics would work if a particular font were loaded, but I
don't yet know which font that is.

If you want IBMgraphics on Linux, then, the only advice I can give is
not to use screen; just use the plain-vanilla Linux console.


